{{/* Managed by ansible (role: openbao_agent). consul-template markup for the bao agent: renders
~/.codex/auth.json from af/dev-workers/codex-auth — the HOST PROJECTION the af-codex-refresh CronJob
publishes after every rotation of the estate's one codex login: access + id token + account_id,
refresh_token already "" server-side. Hosts can read only this projection, never the oauth document,
so no host can ever rotate the shared family (OpenAI refresh tokens are single-use; a second
refresher revokes the family — how every host and the broker lost codex on 2026-09-03). codex 0.153
runs on the stored access_token and never attempts a refresh with an empty refresh_token (verified
2026-09-12, even with a 23-day-old last_refresh). The CronJob rotates every second night and the
agent re-renders within its poll interval, so the token here always has ~8-10 days left. The value
is emitted verbatim (it is already the exact file content). Plain field access on purpose: with
error_on_missing_key it fails the render CLOSED when the field is absent, whereas `index` would
silently render "<no value>" into every host's auth.json (both verified against bao 2.5.5) — which
is also why the projection's field is the dot-free `auth_json`. */ -}}
{{ with secret "af/data/dev-workers/codex-auth" }}{{ .Data.data.auth_json }}{{ end }}
